.\" Written by hand from lib/common.sh (require_config, ignore_pattern, build_exclude_params)
.\" and libexec/archivectl/*.sh; keep it in step with them.
.TH ARCHIVECTL 5 2026-11-15 "archivectl" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
\&.archivectl, .archivectlignore \- backup source configuration and ignore file for archivectl
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I <directory>/.archivectl
.br
.I <directory>/.archivectlignore
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B archivectl init
writes
.I .archivectl
into the directory it is to back up.
Every other command of
.BR archivectl (1)
finds the nearest one in the current directory or its parents, changes
into the directory that holds it, and reads it with the shell's
.B source
builtin: the file is a bash script, run with the user's rights, and may
set any variable.
.PP
These variables are read:
.TP
.B BORG_REPO
The Borg repository, a local path or an
.B ssh://
or scp-style URL.
Required by every command but
.BR init ,
which sets it to
.I $BORG_BACKUP_ROOT/<name>
or the location
.B \-\-repo
gives.
.TP
.B BORG_PASSCOMMAND
The command that prints the passphrase,
.B pass show archivectl/<name>
as
.B init
writes it when it keeps the passphrase in
.BR pass (1);
every command exports it for its borg calls.
.TP
.B BORG_RSH
The command borg reaches another host with, exported for borg when set;
.B init
writes the one set in its environment for a repository on another host.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DIR
What
.B create
archives,
.B diff
compares and
.B restore
extracts into, relative to the directory of the file.
Required by those three;
.B init
sets it to
.BR ./ .
.PP
When no directory at or above the current one holds the file, the
command ends with status 1; a file that leaves a required variable empty
ends it with status 3.
.B init
writes every value quoted for the shell
.RB ( "printf %q" ),
so that a
.BR $ ,
a backquote or a space in a path stays part of it.
.SH IGNORE FILE
.I .archivectlignore
beside
.I .archivectl
lists what
.B create
leaves out and
.B diff
does not compare, one pattern a line, read as
.BR gitignore (5)
reads it: a blank line or one starting with
.B #
is skipped; a name with no
.B /
matches at any depth; a pattern with a
.B /
at the start or inside matches from the source's top; a trailing
.B /
is dropped.
A line starting with a borg pattern style
.RB ( sh: ", " fm: ", " re: ", " pp: ", " pf: )
goes to borg as it is.
Without the file the patterns are
.BR .cache ,
.B tmp
and
.BR __pycache__ .
.B restore
leaves both files as they are.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Backup repository configuration for /home/user/papers
SOURCE_DIR=./
BORG_REPO=/data/backup/borg/home__user__papers
BORG_PASSCOMMAND=pass\e show\e \e'archivectl/home__user__papers\e'
.EE
.PP
.EX
# .archivectlignore
\&.cache
node_modules
*.log
/build/
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR archivectl (1),
.BR borg (1),
.BR pass (1)
